          {
            "field": {
              "type": "ID",
              "value": "summary"
            },
            "fieldType": "summary",
            "type": "SET",
            "value": "OK-to-Design"
          },
          {
            "field": {
              "type": "ID",
              "value": "description"
            },
            "fieldType": "description",
            "type": "SET",
            "value": "Max Degree of Change Going Into Ok-to-Design\n\nForm changes allowable up to 10mm\nHole moves on existing punch planes\nAdded flanges only if contained within current die process\nGage changes within 25%\n\nEP Ok-to-Die Design \n\nMaterial specifications including gage, coating, pre- and post-treat are identified and aligned in FEDEBOM and on the CAD drawing.\nLatest CAD revision level specified on the Body Structures Engineering Authorization for Production Tool Fabrication Kick-Off form.\nMaterial utilization targets should be aligned.\nLocator drawings should be finalized and aligned with the latest CAD level.\nTolerancing and Significant Characteristics should be finalized and any specifications outside the 1294 spec should be called out.\nAll holes and mating surfaces should be finalized with confirmation from cross functional teams. Annotation for holes/slots/cutouts/fasteners/etc. should be finalized and hole groupings should be called out.\nBranding and Part Number Box location should be established and called out.8) \nFor Hot Stamped parts Trim Development Map needed to specify areas of part requiring Hard Trim (Laser Trim not Acceptable)\nGreen feasibility for draw and line dies or, at a minimum, an agreed upon plan by Engineering and Manufacturing to be green by 50% Die Design Review.\nCurrent die process is agreed to by GVT, Cost Estimating and MUD and is able to deliver on all requirements including material utilization, investment and piece price.\nPart costs, both tooling and piece price, is accurate in financial BOM and meets program targets. (If not, a CMF should be generated and approved.)\nAre there any known engineering changes forecasted that may negatively affect the die process or part dimensions (see guidelines on PDP)? If a change is forecasted, can the Ok-to-Design still be authorized with a study file to allow die design to start? If a study file cannot be provided and Ok-to-Design is not authorized, can Program pedigree requirements be met with a delayed Ok-to-Design?"
          },
          {
